postText:
Emergency Conference on EPD's Disaster Preparedness re: Typhoon ''Rolly''

PMGEN DEBOLD M SINAS, RD, NCRPO together with PBGEN FLORENCIO T ORTILLA, DRDO and PBGEN JOHNSON C ALMAZAN, DD, EPD holds an Emergency Meeting on EPD's Preparation for Security, Safety, and Response Operations re: Typhoon ''Rolly'' attended by R-Staffs, Command Group, D-Staffs, COPs, PaMaMariSan, Force Commander, DMFB, and other Senior Officers earlier this morning at EPD Conference Room, Caruncho Avenue, Pasig City. 

The Eastern Police District is ramping up its preparation for the onslaught of Typhoon ''Rolly'' by mobilizing and activating its Reactionary Standby Support Force (RSSF) and Search and Rescue (SAR) team to ensure readiness for possible deployment. 

Hence, RD, NCRPO directed all Stations and Force Battallion to ensure preparedness and response operation  in areas threatened  by the destructive effects of the Typhoon ''Rolly'' and are expected to conduct the following activities:
-Ensure readiness of the Search and Rescue equipment and supplies;
-Conduct routine patrols to high risk areas;
-Disseminate public warnings through Oplan Bandillo;
-Establish Checkpoint Operations to all identified entry/exit points during force evacuation of the residents to flood prone areas; 
-Ready to conduct relief operations;
-Continuous monitoring on the current situation;  
-Coordinate with the City Disaster Risk Reduction Management Office (CDRRMO) for appropriate actions to ensure the safety and security of the public; and
-Implementation of the minimum health protocols to prevent the spread of the virus of CoViD-19.

Meanwhile, RD, NCRPO donated raincoats to be utilized by EPD personnel as they render their duty in the midst of the typhoon. 

#TeamEPDangPaMaMariSan
#ExcelleneProfessionalismDiscipline
